== wcd937x-dt-aoncc [in-progress]
The boot hang (RCU stalls) with the WCD937x patch is the aoncc clock controller at 0x03380000, an SM8250 address with nothing near it in the SM7150 tree: with only aoncc disabled the phone boots (2026-11-09). Without aoncc the VA macro has no mclk, so the macros, SoundWire and the sound card stay deferred. Fix as SM8250 does: no aoncc, VA macro mclk from q6afecc. Audit tools and results in linux-phone-oco/surya-lab and on linux-phone-oco/linux#1.

== microphone [in-progress]
The microphones go through the WCD9375 codec, which the stock device tree does not wire up (the sound card has only the speaker). Needs the device-tree work on linux-phone-oco/linux PR #1 (aoncc dropped, VA macro clocked from q6afecc; built and audited, not yet booted). Test idea: play a tone on the speaker and record it, so the check needs no ears. Boot test needs the user nearby (a hang needs the power button). Prior art found by the kernel-activity feed (2026-11-10): upstream sm7150-mainline committed "WIP WCD stuff" to the surya device tree (7b00a934ace1, 2026-03-28, Aelin Reidel) and reve

